&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You will help the Firefox DOM Core team improve the health of the Session History area. You will write tests to improve the coverage; you will fix tests and/or problems to improve the Gecko correctness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Write Web-Platform tests to improve the coverage, and Gecko mochitests as needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Fix the problems and pass the tests to improve the Gecko correctness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work through code review with the relevant Gecko module owners and iterate to landing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Definition of done&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Improved Session History test coverage and code correctness in Gecko, measured by passed test cases, allowing the team’s senior engineers to focus on security, performance and strategic projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Substantial experience in a browser-engine codebase or in automating for a browser-engine, ideally Firefox/Gecko.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Solid Javascript and applying that language skill to write automated tests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proficiency in and experience developing software in C++.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong debugging skills in a mature larget codebase.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Comfort working in the open: public bugs, code review, and upstream landing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Prior contributions to Gecko or another major browser engine.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with web standards and Web Platform Tests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;WHAT MAKES US EPIC?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the core of Epic’s success are talented, passionate people. Epic prides itself on creating a collaborative, welcoming, and creative environment. Whether it’s building award-winning games or crafting engine technology that enables others to make visually stunning interactive experiences, we’re always innovating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being Epic means being a part of a team that continually strives to do right by our community and users. We’re constantly innovating to raise the bar of engine and game development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ENGINEERING - EPIC GAMES SERVICES&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driving the plug-in power behind Unreal Engine 5. We bridge connections for licensees and our own internal game teams to online services. This allows games like Fortnite to utilize a combination of platform online services as well as Epic’s own online services to build cross-platform online features. Login, parties, voice chat, matchmaking, purchasing, cloud storage, and analytics are just a few examples of online features that our Online Game Services team helps games utilize.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WEB ENGINEER INTERN&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Web Engineer Intern to join the Tools &amp;amp; Portals team within Epic Online Services. Tools &amp;amp; Portals builds the software, platforms, and digital experiences that enable Epic’s internal teams, player support operations, players, and external developers to work with and access Epic services more effectively. You will contribute to production systems across the full stack while gaining hands-on experience with modern web development, backend services, cloud infrastructure, and AI-assisted software development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build full-stack features using React, Next.js, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS with guidance from the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Contribute to development of backend services and APIs using Next.js, NestJS, and Node.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Learn and apply development practices for production infrastructure including AWS, Kubernetes, containers, and CI/CD pipelines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Write, test, review, and deploy production code alongside experienced engineers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Learn and apply AI-assisted software development workflows throughout the software development lifecycle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Contribute to internal tools and developer-facing platforms used across Epic Games&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Interest in full-stack web development and learning modern engineering technologies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Some familiarity with JavaScript, TypeScript, React, or similar web technologies through coursework, projects, or previous experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Eagerness to learn, ask questions, and contribute to solving well-defined engineering problems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Willingness to explore new technologies and codebases, seek support when needed, and incorporate feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ability to work effectively with guidance, communicate questions and blockers, and incorporate feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong collaboration skills and willingness to work closely with engineers, product partners, external teams, and stakeholders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Understanding of defined requirements and willingness to ask clarifying questions when needed&lt;/span

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Analytics Engineer to join our Revenue, Purchase &amp;amp; Order Analytics Engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The area sits at the heart of some of the most critical customer journeys and commercial systems across Vinted’s Marketplace Business Unit, spanning Revenue (pricing and advertising), Purchase (inquiries and checkout), and Orders (transactions and fulfilment). Together, these domains create a rich, high-volume, and deeply interconnected data ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Analytics Engineer, you’ll work at the intersection of data, engineering, and product, building trusted data products that power business and product decision-making across these domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build scalable data products:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, develop, and evolve reliable, cost-efficient data products and pipelines that power analytics and machine learning use cases across the domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build quality in by design:&lt;/strong&gt; Embed automated testing, validation, and quality controls throughout the data lifecycle to ensure data remains accurate, consistent, and complete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen observability:&lt;/strong&gt; Improve monitoring and alerting to detect and address issues before they impact downstream consumers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own production reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Take end-to-end ownership of production data systems, from investigating incidents and diagnosing root causes to implementing durable fixes that prevent recurrence and improve long-term resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you’ll work

&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Build automation that powers the heart of our customers’ most critical operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schuberg Philis, we specialize in mission‑critical IT, partnering closely with our customers to keep their most essential systems running smoothly and securely with 100% responsibility. Our impact is driven by engineers who are deeply technical, automate everything, collaborate naturally, stay curious, take full end‑to‑end ownership, and understand the full stack - from application to core infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for engineers who flourish in automation‑first, mission‑critical environments and want to shape the platforms our customers rely on daily. In a self‑steering customer team, you design, build, run, and improve business‑critical systems across the full stack. You automate everything you touch, streamline pipelines, solve issues across the stack, and tune applications for performance. Working in a culture of real ownership, deep collaboration, and zero silos, where teams carry full responsibility for mission‑critical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;/&amp;nbsp;What you will do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mission‑Critical Automation Engineer, you design, build, run, and improve platforms. You automate everything you touch, diagnose and resolve issues across the entire stack, collaborate closely with customer teams, and take full end‑to‑end ownership of stability, security, and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your day-to-day includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building automation through scripting and configuration management tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the full Plan–Build–Run lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solving multi‑layer issues across OS, network, DB, security, and apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and executing controlled releases with Git and pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform‑hardening practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;/&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;What you bring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong automation mindset, with hands-on experience in advanced scripting and configuration management (e.g. Powershell, Ansible, DSC, Puppet, Chef).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Git and CI/CD practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying security principles in mission-critical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Infrastructure-as-Code tooling such as Terraform, Bicep, or ARM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mentality, combined with curiosity and analytical thinking to understand and improve system behaviour end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of networking, database fundamentals, release/deployment lifecycles, and applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following would be a plus:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and running containerized environments (Docker).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrating platforms using Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operating in public or private cloud environments (Azure, AWS, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
